# No /poc-tauri/ ignore rule on this branch (claude/tauri-poc) - unlike on
# claude/ark-ascended-server-control-a03zpe and main, where poc-tauri/ doesn't exist and that
# line keeps it from ever being accidentally tracked there, this branch's whole point IS the
# poc-tauri/ tree, so ignoring it here would silently stop `git add` from picking up real changes
# (hit exactly that: `git add poc-tauri/...` refused, "ignored by one of your .gitignore files",
# after merging in a commit from that other branch that added the line). Deliberately removed
# here rather than kept as dead weight - a future merge FROM that branch may re-add it, at which
# point it needs removing again rather than left in place.
